---
title: "Paramedic Cardiovascular Care Laboratory"
code: "EMS-222"
category: "emergency-medical-services"
credits: "1"
prerequisites: []
corequisites:
  - "2026/EMS-221"
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisite: Current Virginia EMT and CPR certification as approved by the Virginia Office of EMS."
corequisiteNote: "Corequisite: EMS 221"
---

Focuses on skills involved in the assessment and management of cardiac-related emergencies as outlined by the National Emergency Medical Service Education Standards (NEMSES) for Paramedics. Develops competency in basic dysrhythmia recognition and overall cardiac patient care. Laboratory 2 hours. Total 2 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
